Runtimes and models invoked at execution time
---------------------------------------------

These are not linked into the Go binary. FleetFlow runs them or derives numbers
from them, so they are recorded here.

Eclipse SUMO, including duarouter and netconvert
  Eclipse Public License 2.0. Copyright Eclipse Foundation and the SUMO
  contributors. https://eclipse.dev/sumo/
  FleetFlow invokes `duarouter` and `sumo` as child processes when a SUMO network
  is configured, and reads their trip, route and emission output. SUMO is
  installed separately or in the container image; none of its source or data is
  copied into this repository.

HBEFA3 emission classes, as implemented by SUMO
  The HBEFA3 model is published by TU Graz and INFRAS (Handbook Emission Factors
  for Road Transport). FleetFlow does not reimplement it: when a scenario runs
  through SUMO, the emission class is set in the route file and SUMO returns the
  emission figures. HBEFA3 is named in `internal/simulation/sumo` because that is
  the model SUMO evaluated.

FleetFlow class factors v1
  Original to this project, no third-party rights. The synthetic scenario
  generator's per-class fuel and CO2 factors (`internal/fleet`) are planning
  assumptions written for this repository, not HBEFA3, not a certified
  inventory, and not measured from an operator. The emissions page prints the
  model name it used so the two paths are never confused.

OSRM (Open Source Routing Machine)
  BSD 2-Clause License. Copyright (c) 2016, Project OSRM contributors.
  https://project-osrm.org/
  Route geometry, distance and duration come from an OSRM server that FleetFlow
  queries over HTTP. The server runs separately, from an image built by
  `scripts/osrm`; no OSRM source is vendored here.

Map data and tiles
------------------

The map uses OpenFreeMap tiles with OpenMapTiles and OpenStreetMap attribution.
OpenStreetMap data is © OpenStreetMap contributors and is made available under
the Open Database License (ODbL). The basemap's attribution control displays the
provider and data credits.

The OSRM Jakarta/Jabodetabek extract is downloaded from Geofabrik
(https://download.geofabrik.de/asia/indonesia.html) and is derived from
OpenStreetMap, so it carries the same ODbL obligations: attribution to
OpenStreetMap contributors, and share-alike for any derived database that is
published. The extract and the OSRM graph built from it stay under `data/osrm/`,
which is ignored by Git, and are not redistributed by this repository.

Emission factors reference no third-party data set; the figures in
`internal/fleet` are stated assumptions with their sources named in the code.

